 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 121 people. Revenue per employee of $8.0M ranks in the top quartile among Real Estate peers, improving at 15%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $213K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Medical Properties Trust, Inc. is a small-cap real estate business with a $1.1B market cap on $972M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -14% over the past three years and +8% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 2% against a 6% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 16.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 20.7% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 8.8% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (33.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Real Estate peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"t